      "writtenOn": "2023-05-18T08:28:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we do these only if isLocalOnly is false? I know that the LOHS APIs only support wifi, but the TetheringManager system APIs do support things like TETHERING_ETHERNET + CONNECTIVITY_SCOPE_LOCAL, right. So something like:\n\n    if (!isLocalOnly) {\n        if (mStaticIpv4ServerAddr !\u003d null) return mStaticIpv4ServerAddr;\n\n        if (shouldNotConfigureBluetoothInterface()) return new LinkAddress(BLUETOOTH_IFACE_ADDR);\n    }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 684,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 686,
        "endChar": 97
      },
      "revId": "1df3bab29fcda1fae6491c610554a3283695116a",
